title: "Wildfire-RL: Geospatial Reinforcement Learning for Wildfire Suppression and Cross-Regional Policy Transfer"
authors:
  - family-names: Akarma
    given-names: Ali
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-06-26"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/aliakarma/wildfire-rl"
keywords:
  - reinforcement-learning
  - wildfire
  - ppo
  - transfer-learning
  - multi-agent-reinforcement-learning
  - geospatial
  - remote-sensing
  - domain-generalization
abstract: >
  Wildfire-RL is a reproducible framework and benchmark for training proximal-policy-
  optimization (PPO) agents to suppress wildfires on geospatial state tensors built from
  ERA5 climate, SRTM terrain, MODIS NDVI fuel, and FIRMS ignition data. It supports
  single-agent and centralized cooperative multi-agent control, ablation studies,
  multi-seed statistical evaluation, and a symmetric cross-regional transfer protocol
  between desert (Saudi Eastern Province) and forest (Northern California) wildfire regimes.
